<title>USA: CMS Energy 142,000 customers lose power.</title>
<headline>CMS Energy 142,000 customers lose power.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Mich. 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consumers Energy Co said Friday an ice storm cut off power overnight to about 175,000 of its electric customers, and about 142,000 are still without power.</p>
<p>Consumers Energy, the main utility unit of CMS Energy Corp said customers affected included 30,000 in Jackson, 25,000 in Kalamazoo, 19,000 in Battle Creek, 11,000 in Jonesville, 11,000 in Adrian; 8,000 in Lansing, 7,000 in Flint, 5,000 in southern Monroe County; 4,000 in Bronson and 200 in Owosso.</p>
</text>
